ALVA — Complete Super Jump Movement Overhaul

Primary Objective

Implement a complete, polished, production-ready overhaul of Alva’s universal jumping mechanics.

Replace the existing “hold Jump to jump higher” mechanic with a new movement action called “Super Jump.”

The new mechanics must work identically for human-controlled and CPU-controlled fighters, respecting Alva’s shared movement architecture.

Required new controls

Action	Input	Result
Normal Jump	Press Jump while grounded	A noticeably lower, compact jump
Super Jump	Hold Down, then press Jump while grounded	A dramatically stronger upward leap
Air Jump	Press Jump while airborne	Uses one of the two existing air jumps
Fast Fall	Hold Down while descending	Accelerates descent as before

The fundamental requirement is that Super Jump must feel like a powerful leap, not merely a normal jump that floats higher.

Super Jump must also produce a distinctive ground-level dust burst at takeoff.

Critical height requirement

Alva’s previous higher jump must become Super Jump, with approximately the same maximum height it had before this update.

Do not substantially increase or decrease that height.

Normal jumps, however, must become noticeably shorter than before, establishing a much clearer distinction between the two movement options.

Do not confuse this requirement with any previous proposal in the repository’s max file that suggests increasing Super Jump height to approximately 328 units. That is not the requested balance.

