7. Preserve the Previous Higher Jump’s Height as Super Jump

This is equally important.

The current higher jump has an idealized maximum height near:

169 × 1.4 ≈ 237 world units

Super Jump should reach approximately this same height.

Do not make it significantly taller.

Record the original baseline first

Before removing the old mechanic:

1. Use the existing movement test harness.
2. Measure the actual old higher-jump apex.
3. Record its displacement from takeoff.
4. Use that measured value as the regression target for Super Jump.

The actual simulated height matters more than the simplified physics formula because Alva integrates movement at fixed simulation steps.

New universal configuration

Introduce a dedicated shared parameter:

superJumpVelocity

A reasonable initial value is approximately:

jumpVelocity: 740,
superJumpVelocity: 1100

Adjust superJumpVelocity against the measured baseline until Super Jump’s apex closely matches the former higher jump.

Target approximately ±5–8 world units of the old higher jump, preferably tighter if achievable.

The final movement configuration should be centralized in:

js/data/movement.js

No character definition should override these parameters.

Desired height relationship

The final distinction should resemble:

Jump type	Approximate apex
Previous Normal Jump	169 units
New Normal Jump	100–115 units
Previous Higher Jump	237 units
New Super Jump	Approximately 237 units

This establishes a noticeably stronger contrast without increasing the game’s overall intended vertical reach.

