Final Design Direction

The finished system should create three clearly different jumping experiences:

Normal Jump: A quick, low, responsive hop used for ordinary movement and combat positioning.

Super Jump: A deliberate Down + Jump command that propels the fighter powerfully upward, reaches the original higher jump’s height, and creates a satisfying dust explosion at the feet.

Air Jump: The familiar additional midair jump, preserving Alva’s existing triple-jump and recovery gameplay.

Most importantly, Super Jump should feel powerful because of the initial leap, its immediate vertical acceleration, and its takeoff presentation—not because the fighter floats under reduced gravity.

Players and CPUs must obey the same rules, use the same movement system, and have access to the same mechanic.

Implement the complete change across gameplay, presentation, CPU intelligence, UI, documentation, and tests rather than stopping after the basic jump-physics modification.
